# Build output
mod.ff
tools/dist/
# The custom-image delivery zip (images/*.iwi packed for FastDL). Nothing on THIS branch builds
# it — make_iwd.ps1 and deploy.ps1's New-ModIwd live with the camo work — but the artifact is a
# repo-root file that survives a branch switch (git never touches untracked files), so without
# this rule it sits here as `??`, one `git add .` away from committing a 389KB binary this branch
# does not even use. GLOB, because a rebuild against a RUNNING game cannot overwrite the mounted
# .iwd and falls back to writing `mp_gunfight.iwd.new` beside it.
mp_gunfight.iwd*

# Offline research scratch: inflated map fastfiles (hundreds of MB of binary dumps) written by
# tools/inflate_fastfile_zlib.ps1. The catalogs it FEEDS (tools/wager_spawns, tools/wager_entities)
# are small JSON and ARE tracked, so the extraction never has to be repeated -- only the raw
# intermediates are disposable. tools/README.md has claimed this was ignored since 2026-06; it
# wasn't, until now.
tools/ff_extract/

# Runtime/log output
*.log
*.log.*
missingasset.csv
__converter/
demos/
imgui.ini
main/
players/
plutonium/
zone/

# Claude Code — local permissions (machine-specific paths)
.claude/settings.json
.claude/settings.local.json

# Join notifier — real config carries the secret ntfy topic (acts like a password)
tools/notify/config.json

# Box-local "mute from the activity surfaces" list (status_service + join-notify read it).
# Holds player GUIDs — account identifiers, and this repo is public. Template is .example
tools/ignore.local.json

# Player GUID -> Discord user id, so a join alert can name someone in Discord. Same class as
# ignore.local.json above and blocked for the same reason: it is KEYED by player GUID, which
# the address/PII rule keeps out of every tracked file. The committed template is
# tools/players.example.json and it carries invented values only.
tools/players.local.json

# RCON panel — real rcon_password store (per-profile). Never commit; template is .example
# GLOB, not the exact path: `secrets.local.json.bak` (a routine editor backup) used to slip past
# all three layers at once — this ignore, the pre-commit `case`, and the packagers' drop-list —
# and would then have been BUNDLED by package_server.ps1 -IncludeRconTool, carrying live rcon
# passwords to another box. The !…example negation keeps the template committable.
tools/rcon/secrets.local.*
!tools/rcon/secrets.local.*.example

# RCON panel — profile list: names + REAL hosts/ports (incl. the VPS public IP). Split out of
# secrets.local.json so a host/port edit never touches the password store, and so no public IP
# ships in the committed tree. Joined to the password store BY PROFILE NAME — rename a profile
# in one file and the panel shows the server but cannot auth. Never commit; template is .example
# Same GLOB + negation as the password store above, and for the same near-miss-filename reason.
tools/rcon/servers.local.*
!tools/rcon/servers.local.*.example

# RCON panel — box-local UI state (the FAVORITES pinboard). Lives with the PANEL, not the browser,
# so the VPS panel shows one pinboard over RDP and over the SSH tunnel alike. Regenerated on demand.
tools/rcon/prefs.local.json

# RCON panel — learned per-server cache of dvars the game server rejects as "Unknown command"
# (so the connect-sweep stops bare-sending them). Machine/server-specific; regenerated on demand.
tools/rcon/.dvarcache.json

# RCON panel — geo lookup cache (player IP -> country/city, from ip-api.com). PII: it maps real
# player IPs to locations, so it stays on the box and never enters git or a web root. Only the
# 2-letter country code derived from it is ever published. Regenerated on demand.
tools/rcon/.geocache.json

# Ops crib sheet — the REAL addresses docs/ now carries as <admin-home-ip> / <vnc-console-ip>
# placeholders (home egress IP, Contabo VNC console). This is precisely what the doc redactions
# + the pre-commit IP guard exist to keep out of git, so the ignore is a GLOB: it must hold whether
# the file lands as .json or .md. The !…example negation keeps a committable template possible
# (same pattern as server/*.cfg below). Box/operator-local; nothing reads it but a human.
tools/ops.local.*
!tools/ops.local.*.example

# Security watcher — what it TRUSTS (ssh key fingerprints, users). Box-identifying, and this
# repo is public. Optional file; template is .example
tools/security.local.json

# Security watcher — box-local bookmarks + the learned baseline (event RecordIds, authorized_keys
# hash, firewall posture). Regenerated on demand; deleting it re-runs trust-on-first-use.
tools/vps_services/security_state.json

# Watchdog — box-local alert-state (down/recovered transitions), regenerated on demand
tools/vps_services/watchdog_state.json

# Watchdog — self-expiring maintenance marker written by deploy.ps1 to mute alerts during a
# planned restart; box-local, always transient
tools/vps_services/watchdog_maintenance.json

# Loadout editor — rolling backup written next to the edited .gsc on each save
*.editorbak

# Local-only reference/server files
dedicated.cfg
dedicated_sp.cfg
# Server cfgs: block any real/live cfg (carries rcon_password) but allow sanitized templates.
server/*.cfg
!server/*.cfg.example
gsc resources/
# raw/ is ignored as a class (engine-dump copies, build_ff staging residue) — but the mod's OWN
# custom FX sources live at raw/fx/misc/*.efx and MUST be tracked (they exist nowhere else; a
# fresh clone rebuilds mod.ff from them). A bare `!raw/fx/misc/*.efx` would be dead — git never
# descends into an ignored directory — so each parent dir is re-included on the way down.
raw/*
!raw/fx/
raw/fx/*
!raw/fx/misc/
raw/fx/misc/*
!raw/fx/misc/*.efx
tools/ff_extract/
# material_spike WORKSPACE artifacts (tools/material_spike/README.md): make_material.ps1
# writes the triplet at the repo root for build_ff staging. Transient until a spike asset
# goes to production -- the repo IS the mod folder, so a committed images/ deploys to the
# VPS and FastDL. Lift these deliberately at that point, never by accident.
# Same treatment as images\ below: the camo CARRIER materials are production sources (mod.csv
# registers them, and without them the camo images never load), so they are tracked. Spike
# scratch under these dirs stays ignored.
materials/*
!materials/gf_camo_*_mtl
material_properties/*
!material_properties/gf_camo_*_mtl
# ⚠ images\ is NO LONGER blanket-ignored -- the custom weapon camos went to production
# 2026-08-16 and their .iwi files are the SOURCE OF TRUTH (nothing regenerates them but
# tools/make_camo_iwi.ps1 with the exact seed/preset, and mp_gunfight.iwd is built FROM them).
# Written as `images/*` + a negation, not `images/`, because git cannot re-include a file whose
# PARENT DIRECTORY is excluded -- with the old `images/` line the `!` below would never match.
# Spike scratch (gf_test.iwi and friends) stays ignored; only gf_camo_* is tracked.
images/*
!images/gf_camo_*.iwi
# ⚠ A RESIDENT-OVERRIDE image is named after the STOCK asset it replaces, so it does NOT match the
# gf_camo_* negation above and would be silently left behind. That is a DEPLOY bug, not a cosmetic
# one: deploy.ps1 builds mp_gunfight.iwd on the box FROM this directory, so an untracked override
# is absent from the VPS clone, absent from its .iwd, and the live server quietly serves the stock
# texture while the laptop looks correct. Track every override explicitly.
!images/camo_gold_*.iwi
# Build artifact: the .iwd is just images/*.iwi zipped for delivery. Regenerated on demand.
# GLOB, not the exact name: a RUNNING GAME holds the .iwd open (Plutonium mounts it and keeps the
# handle), so make_iwd.ps1 falls back to writing `mp_gunfight.iwd.new` beside the live file for the
# caller to swap in. The exact-name rule left that sibling untracked-but-unignored, i.e. permanent
# `??` clutter that also invites committing a build output. Same near-miss-filename reasoning as
# the secrets.local.* glob above.
mp_gunfight.iwd*
# ⚠ shelved/ is DELIBERATELY TRACKED (no rule here excludes it). Parked work-in-progress plus
# its restore checklist -- it has to survive a clone to be worth anything. The ignore rules
# above are path-anchored to the repo ROOT, so a shelved copy of images/ or materials/ is
# unaffected by them.

# Discord live-status card - the remembered message id it keeps rewriting. Box-local and
# per-channel: copying it to another box would make that box edit THIS box's card. Regenerated
# on demand (a missing id just posts a fresh card, and the old one is then orphaned).
tools/notify/discord_status.local.json
